Your SCBA facepiece is one of the most handled pieces of equipment on the rig. It takes constant abuse from heat, soot, and repeated donning and doffing, so a consistent cleaning routine extends lens life and keeps the valves working as designed. This guide covers the basics our service technicians recommend for departments of any size.

{INJECTION}

After each use, rinse the facepiece in lukewarm water with a mild, pH-neutral detergent. Avoid alcohol-based wipes on the lens, since they can cloud polycarbonate over time. Let the unit air dry away from direct sunlight and heaters. Once dry, inspect the head harness straps for cracking or loss of elasticity and replace any strap that no longer springs back. Log each cleaning in the equipment record so annual flow testing has a complete history. Store facepieces in a soft bag rather than loose in a compartment to prevent scratches. If you find a sticky inhalation valve or a torn nose cup, tag the unit out of service and contact an authorized service center.
